course: dictionary
lesson: 4585
title: Half of a big ball
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A hemisphere is half of a sphere, which is a ball shape. The word has two parts, and both tell you something: hemi means half, and sphere means ball. So when you read hemisphere, think "half of a round thing".
explain: The equator is an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth. It splits the Earth into two hemispheres. «About two-thirds of the Earth's land lies in the northern hemisphere.» The word northern is the clue: it names the top half, so a hemisphere here is the top half of the Earth.
explain: Context can also show you what happens in a hemisphere. «Australia and New Zealand are in the Southern Hemisphere, so their seasons are upside down.» The word so tells you the seasons are different because of where they are. Try the swap test: "Australia is in the bottom half of the Earth" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A hemisphere is half of a sphere, a ball shape.
fact: The equator divides the Earth into the Northern Hemisphere and the Southern Hemisphere.
fact: When it is summer in one hemisphere, it is winter in the other.
fact: «Australia and New Zealand are in the Southern Hemisphere.»
fact: Your brain has two hemispheres: a left hemisphere and a right hemisphere.
exercise: A hemisphere is half of what? | A tree | A square | A river | *A sphere, which is a ball shape
exercise: «About two-thirds of the Earth's land lies in the northern hemisphere.» Which half of the Earth is this? | *The Northern Hemisphere | Both halves at once | The Southern Hemisphere | The left hemisphere of the brain
exercise: «Australia and New Zealand are in the Southern Hemisphere, so their seasons are upside down.» What does upside down mean here? | They have the same seasons as the north | Their seasons change every hour | *Their seasons are the opposite of the seasons in the north | They have no seasons at all
test: In the Southern Hemisphere, which months are summer months? | March, April and May | June, July and August | *December, January and February | September, October and November
test: The brain has two halves. What is each half called? | A pole | A sphere | An equator | *A hemisphere
exam: Which imaginary line splits the Earth into the Northern Hemisphere and the Southern Hemisphere? | The horizon | *The equator | A line of mountains | A river
